    "problem_statement": "Action functions executed twice when using retry decorators\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using tenacity retry decorators, action functions (like `before_sleep`, `after_attempt`, etc.) are being executed twice per retry attempt instead of once. This causes unexpected behavior where callbacks are invoked multiple times.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport tenacity\n\ncall_count = 0\n\ndef my_callback(retry_state):\n    global call_count\n    call_count += 1\n    print(f\"Callback called {call_count} times\")\n\n@tenacity.retry(\n    stop=tenacity.stop_after_attempt(3),\n    wait=tenacity.wait_fixed(0.1),\n    before_sleep=my_callback\n)\ndef failing_function():\n    raise ValueError(\"This always fails\")\n\ntry:\n    failing_function()\nexcept tenacity.RetryError:\n    pass\n\nprint(f\"Expected 2 calls, got {call_count} calls\")\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nCallback called 1 times\nCallback called 2 times\nExpected 2 calls, got 2 calls\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nCallback called 1 times\nCallback called 2 times\nCallback called 3 times\nCallback called 4 times\nExpected 2 calls, got 4 calls\n```\n\nThe same issue occurs with other action functions like `after_attempt` and retry error callbacks."
  },
